  "contract": [
    "Host::functions is the stable authority for Rust callbacks and name/arity/global descriptors; host_functions! derives records.",
    "Guest callables use the existing Native environment with a private operation index, without a second registry or heap category.",
    "NativeContext roots receiver, arguments, results and exceptions for the callback lifetime. Drop releases scoped roots; retain explicitly promotes host-owned roots.",
    "Re-entry uses existing VM property/call/program/realm semantics and the shared retained-error operation.",
    "Return and exception roots validate owner/generation before crossing the callback boundary; raw exceptions without a validated root are not trusted.",
    "Fresh execution invalidates retained handles. Native functions are currently nonconstructible; native classes remain open."
  ],
  "internal_obligations_verified": [
    "Borrowed callback inputs/results expire; promoted handles preserve identity through collection and expire on fresh execution.",
    "Dynamic callable re-entry preserves program ownership; guest and native throws retain actual objects through collection and scope exit.",
    "Foreign and released success/exception handles reject; invalid returns still release borrowed scopes; unknown operation indices reject."
  ],
